<BaseLayout title="Transit: A CARS Reading Practice Project | Will Chai" description="Transit is William Chai’s reading endurance project for MCAT CARS preparation, using generated passages inspired by a reader’s interests." path="/transit-a-cars-endurance-training-tool/"><div class="pageShell"><SiteHeader current="projects" /><main id="main" class="pageMain"><article class="archiveRecord"><p>Project archive · William Chai</p><h1>Transit: A CARS Reading Practice Project</h1><section><h2>Reading practice</h2><p>Transit was a reading practice project by William Chai for the Critical Analysis and Reasoning Skills section of the MCAT. It generated dense passages inspired by topics the reader found interesting.</p></section><section><h2>How the project worked</h2><p>The design used modules for a fictional author, passage writing and editorial direction. Readers practised identifying a position, following an argument and maintaining attention through complex prose.</p></section><section><h2>Project scope</h2><p>The original tool generated passages for supplementary reading practice. Its generated authors and citations could be fictional. Official AAMC resources remained part of the preparation process. This page records the project and its approach; the interactive generator belongs to the original application.</p></section><p><a href="mailto:me@willchai.com">Contact William Chai</a> · <a href="/projects/">Current projects</a> · <a href="/resume/">Résumé</a></p></article></main><SiteFooter /></div></BaseLayout>
